  "historical_output_text": " Hi Jane,\nSo just walking down on our way into grocery today, the cherry blossom trees in our neighbor garden started dropping petals like confederates in May 58. Just like a carpet! I stopped to snap some quick pic.\nI just want u to experience what beauty we got around.\nHope it makes it into next week for u to appreciate!\nCheers!\n\nPete\n\n---\n\n---\n\nHi Peter,\n\nThank so, the petals were like a rainbow on the ground under my nose. Such beautiful colors! Thanks so, for reminding to stop and admire nature. Can't get too excited with this pandemic going, and we are still waiting to go outside more often.\n\nBest regards,  \n\n Jane Hi Jane!\nSo great that I got a thumbs for this, you are so in sync with what beauty means. And it feels great you enjoyed the petals!",
